      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "The marble has fallen perfectly for smart filly WILLOWS GIRL (1). She came from much wider for a resuming win at Melton and put together a string of wins last campaign including the Gold Bracelet and a NSW Oaks heat. The inside draw should see her very hard to stop. SEASIDE BOULEVARD (9) makes her first appearance since a second in July's Queensland Oaks having earlier claimed the Redcliffe Oaks. Draws for a trail and was readied with a trial. Nutrien Classic winner EYE WISH (11) added to a strong record at this circuit and distance with a second-up win last time. Tricky draw but should be hitting her peak. GO EASY ON ME (10) is another that may require luck from the back line but she has been good so far this time in, winning fresh in the city before a second against the older males last start.",
